{"event_type":"review","id":"cb03674eb4e934b72e3df70cac1f48dad446bef6df7480cd4203a6c1a499175f","occurred_at":"2026-11-07T18:32:52Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/3e5dd6ff393ce12ba244d69ffaad5ed15d630efd14573e6c1b78aec528e462e4","sha256":"3e5dd6ff393ce12ba244d69ffaad5ed15d630efd14573e6c1b78aec528e462e4"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/0c753a77bb580425cc74e9ea76fa5a6db73753489a81de6300a5fcac04f86820","sha256":"0c753a77bb580425cc74e9ea76fa5a6db73753489a81de6300a5fcac04f86820"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/1ca02906258fa9d0f5365cad96551b4c8d975d49cd61078370d435fb8cf527de","sha256":"1ca02906258fa9d0f5365cad96551b4c8d975d49cd61078370d435fb8cf527de"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/66ebd9b3b0370c9d7cac8ba15ba0a0593691cbe4f1e75973f871c68cb2ae6c56","sha256":"66ebd9b3b0370c9d7cac8ba15ba0a0593691cbe4f1e75973f871c68cb2ae6c56"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/f316b0fd6e586683471679ece966b36123890c91131c5274829c0b5cc0896074","sha256":"f316b0fd6e586683471679ece966b36123890c91131c5274829c0b5cc0896074"}],"attempt_id":"51e79a6d696dcaeeebf429e828e68f45c14f01d15c0a14afc8849c277545ca72:0:1","base":"004033448a23af20af90a9a313f3bd4caf516a4a","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"07b5b96471dc34e12a82a522fa5d11a4d5f9531f","body":"**`timestamp` accepts non-ASCII digits.**\n\n- In Python `str` regexes, `\\d` matches any Unicode decimal digit, so a value like `\"٢٠٢٦-10-31T00:00:00Z\"` passes the check at review_ledger.py:100. `strptime` also accepts it.\n- The same instant then has more than one valid spelling. Each spelling hashes to a different event `id`, which breaks the canonical-evidence assumption.\n- The raw string is also passed as `GIT_AUTHOR_DATE` and `GIT_COMMITTER_DATE` (review_ledger.py:586). If git rejects it at `commit-tree`, the error is outside the push `try`. Every later `publish` call then fails on the same spooled event, and the outbox stays blocked.\n\nRestrict the check to ASCII digits. If the `occurred_at` pattern in the checked-in schema uses `\\d`, restrict it the same way.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-    if not isinstance(value, str) or not re.fullmatch(r\"\\d{4}-\\d\\d-\\d\\dT\\d\\d:\\d\\d:\\d\\dZ\", value):\n+    if not isinstance(value, str) or not re.fullmatch(r\"[0-9]{4}-[0-9]{2}-[0-9]{2}T[0-9]{2}:[0-9]{2}:[0-9]{2}Z\", value):\n```\n</details>","id":"07ac4af29f5d019d3b88888edbe7009cf708562d2616554e8f329f27aea11e2a","intervals":[],"path":"apps/crq-python/review_ledger.py","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"`timestamp` accepts non-ASCII digits."},{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"07b5b96471dc34e12a82a522fa5d11a4d5f9531f","body":"**`publish` treats final push refusals as transient and hides their cause.**\n\n- `IntegrityError` is a subclass of `ValueError` (review_ledger.py:55). The `except` at review_ledger.py:595 therefore catches the bundle-size refusal raised at review_ledger.py:423.\n- The same `except` catches the signer's own `ValueError` refusals, such as \"base moved\", \"independent\", \"count bound\" and \"aggregate size\" (see test_signer_ledger.py:95-140).\n- These refusals give the same result on every retry. Each retry still builds a new bundle and makes another signer call, so another token is minted.\n- After `attempts`, the caller only sees \"publication pending; retain scope ownership and reconcile\". The specific cause is lost.\n\nThe ledger still fails closed. The impact is a lost diagnostic plus up to `attempts` wasted publish round-trips. The fix: let local `IntegrityError` propagate, and chain the last push error into the final raise.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n+                last_error = None\n                 for batch in groups:\n@@\n                     try:\n                         self.push(head, commit)\n-                    except (subprocess.SubprocessError, OSError, ValueError, RuntimeError):\n+                    except IntegrityError:\n+                        raise\n+                    except (subprocess.SubprocessError, OSError, ValueError, RuntimeError) as exc:\n+                        last_error = exc\n                         break  # Includes timeout after push: next fetch reconciles.\n```\n\nThen define `last_error = None` before the `for _ in range(attempts)` loop, and change the final raise to:\n\n```python\nraise IntegrityError(\"publication pending; retain scope ownership and reconcile\") from last_error\n```\n</details>","id":"d49673bf29d79d627a41c1784102777766cd071d1caae8942500ce5ac722f4e2","intervals":[],"path":"apps/crq-python/review_ledger.py","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"`publish` treats final push refusals as transient and hides their cause."},{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"dcf42b20bd24c39c43dc2d0165c847f67c4e8eb1","body":"**Move the ledger fetch outside `tick.lock`.**\n\n`select()` calls `GitLedger.fetch()` before the quota-refusal shortcut. A slow remote can hold `tick.lock` for up to 300 seconds per fetch and delay other tick work.\n\nFetch and validate the ledger off-lock. Have selection use a fresh validated head and events snapshot, and defer selection when it is missing or stale.","id":"dfb501e57def4de44ba5db43292e6adcce8aa7108b032b222cf3f4c74df488d1","intervals":[],"path":"apps/crq-python/backfill_runtime.py","severity":"major","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Move the ledger fetch outside `tick.lock`."}],"head":"47ff1cde251156fad487f9c54d67799bc7c99f0b","head_tree":"067d49da10942551a3c39da201ad1d79467f9afa","input_scope":[{"blob":"dcf42b20bd24c39c43dc2d0165c847f67c4e8eb1","intervals":[[1,597]],"path":"apps/crq-python/backfill_runtime.py"},{"blob":"c28b6d2fcda32b1035a95f45d9fed8bfe534af9d","intervals":[[1,374]],"path":"apps/crq-python/push_current.py"},{"blob":"772df561b2a8264b8f38bd5d1371c055235b7ae4","intervals":[[1,562]],"path":"apps/crq-python/repair_tick.py"},{"blob":"07b5b96471dc34e12a82a522fa5d11a4d5f9531f","intervals":[[1,603]],"path":"apps/crq-python/review_ledger.py"},{"blob":"0244806bac667b2dcc424b8383951bf7e50b214e","intervals":[[1,352]],"path":"apps/crq-python/test_crq_coverage.py"},{"blob":"7e33071e0283795db6c27aee4344c904a2208b44","intervals":[[1,226]],"path":"apps/crq-python/test_deploy_controller_cli.py"},{"blob":"7369dc46204e3da7e584a21204605246a3bc1414","intervals":[[1,522]],"path":"apps/crq-python/test_repair_drain.py"},{"blob":"33b5a129689ac6559f54e3b4d4e8f7fb1eece8c4","intervals":[[1,337]],"path":"apps/crq-python/test_signer_ledger.py"}],"job_id":"51e79a6d696dcaeeebf429e828e68f45c14f01d15c0a14afc8849c277545ca72:0","outcome":"completed","paths":[{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path cluster"},"blob":"dcf42b20bd24c39c43dc2d0165c847f67c4e8eb1","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"apps/crq-python/backfill_runtime.py","reason":"bounded verified input"},{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path cluster"},"blob":"c28b6d2fcda32b1035a95f45d9fed8bfe534af9d","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"apps/crq-python/push_current.py","reason":"bounded verified input"},{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path cluster"},"blob":"772df561b2a8264b8f38bd5d1371c055235b7ae4","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"apps/crq-python/repair_tick.py","reason":"bounded verified input"},{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path cluster"},"blob":"07b5b96471dc34e12a82a522fa5d11a4d5f9531f","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"apps/crq-python/review_ledger.py","reason":"bounded verified input"},{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path cluster"},"blob":"0244806bac667b2dcc424b8383951bf7e50b214e","disposition":"includ